---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="privacy · tracelane"
  description="what tracelane.dev collects, what it doesn't, and how we handle the few things we do."
>
  <section class="container-prose py-24">
    <p class="font-mono text-xs text-fg-dim mb-4 tracking-wider lowercase">
      privacy policy
    </p>
    <h1
      class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lowercase"
    >
      privacy.
    </h1>
    <p class="mt-6 text-lg text-fg-muted leading-relaxed">
      this page covers tracelane.dev — the marketing site. the product
      (gateway, dashboard, docs) has separate documentation at
      docs.tracelane.dev/privacy.
    </p>

    <h2
      class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lowercase"
    >
      what we collect on tracelane.dev
    </h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted lowercase">
      <li>— your email address, if you submit the notify form.</li>
      <li>— your IP country (two-letter code, from Cloudflare's CF-IPCountry header) and a truncated User-Agent string, stored alongside your email for abuse detection only.</li>
      <li>— Cloudflare Web Analytics aggregate data: page views, referrer, geographic region. server-side beacon, no cookies set in your browser.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2
      class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lowercase"
    >
      what we don't collect
    </h2>
    <ul class="mt-4 space-y-2 text-fg-muted lowercase">
      <li>— no cookies are set by tracelane.dev. nothing in your browser to delete.</li>
      <li>— no third-party trackers. no Google Analytics. no Plausible JS. no Segment. no HubSpot. no Marketo. no Intercom widget.</li>
      <li>— no marketing automation, no email re-engagement, no lead-scoring.</li>
      <li>— no fingerprinting.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2
      class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lowercase"
    >
      how we use your email
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted lowercase leading-relaxed">
      one email on June 16, 2026 — the v1 launch notification. if you don't
      explicitly opt into product updates after that, you'll never hear from us
      again. we do not sell or share your email with any third party.
    </p>

    <h2
      class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lowercase"
    >
      where your data lives
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted lowercase leading-relaxed">
      the notify form writes to a Cloudflare D1 database, region-pinned to
      Cloudflare's nearest edge to the submitter. data is not replicated
      cross-region. we do not export this data to any third-party tool.
    </p>

    <h2
      class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lowercase"
    >
      your rights
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted lowercase leading-relaxed">
      email <code class="font-mono text-fg">support@tracelane.dev</code> to
      request deletion of your email address from the notify list. we'll
      action it within 7 days. GDPR data-subject requests and DPDP rights
      requests get the same treatment.
    </p>

    <h2
      class="mt-16 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-fg lowercase"
    >
      changes
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-fg-muted lowercase leading-relaxed">
      this policy may change. if it changes materially, anyone on the notify
      list will get a single email explaining what changed before the change
      takes effect.
    </p>

    <p class="mt-16 text-sm text-fg-subtle lowercase">
      last updated: may 20, 2026.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
